  Covers files with the .MoodSetting.xml extension (class CPlugMoodSetting): the lighting,
  sky, fog and post-processing of one mood. See moodblender.xsd for .MoodBlender.xml.

  Use:
    <Mood xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="moodsetting.xsd">

  How the engine handles a document:
    * The name of the root element is not checked. The game writes <Mood>, and this schema
      accepts only that.
    * Element and attribute names are case-sensitive. Child elements may be in any order. If one
      is repeated, the first is used.
    * Unknown elements, attributes and text are silently ignored. This schema reports them.
    * A missing required element or attribute, or a value that cannot be read, is logged as a
      data error. The value keeps its default and loading continues.
    * Numbers outside their range are clamped without any error. This schema reports them.
    * Unrecognized boolean text reads as false without any error. This schema reports it.
    * Some attributes are read only to convert older files. They are marked "Legacy".

  Sources in the binary (image base 140000000):
